s have been received from each entity.", "clarity_score": 5, "needs_manual_review": false, "source_reference": "Article 14(1)(B)"}], "controls": [{"control_title": "AML/CFT Policy Framework Maintenance and Senior Management Approval", "control_objective": "Ensure a comprehensive, proportionate, and senior-management-approved AML/CFT policy framework is in place and effectively implemented at all times.", "control_description": "Compliance owns the AML/CFT policy framework, which comprises the overarching AML/CFT policy and all subsidiary procedures. The framework is reviewed at least annually and updated to reflect changes in the regulatory environment, risk assessment outcomes, and business activities. Every version is formally approved by the Board or designated senior management committee before publication and is distributed to all relevant staff with an attestation mechanism to confirm receipt and understanding.", "control_owner": "Compliance", "control_type": "Preventive", "execution_type": "Manual", "frequency": "Annual + Event-Driven", "control_level": "Policy", "evidence_generated": "Board/senior management approval minutes or signed approval page; policy version register; staff attestation records", "key_steps": ["Compliance initiates the annual policy review cycle, comparing the existing framework against current regulatory requirements and the latest risk assessment findings.", "Proposed changes are drafted and circulated to relevant business units for comment.", "Revised policy is submitted to the Board or AML Committee for formal approval; the signed approval record is retained.", "Approved policy is published on the internal intranet and distributed to all relevant staff; attestation of receipt and understanding is collected and tracked.", "Compliance monitors effective implementation through scheduled control testing; findings are reported to senior management quarterly."], "residual_risk_if_failed": "High"}, {"control_title": "Group-Wide AML Policy 